T RenderSchedule             | RenderSchedule.h | 94-126 | owning                        | -  | The ordered recordings of one rotation, fixed at bring-up and merely executed per rotation. implies a solved dependency structure Slate does not build. The recordings and the target set are both known at bring-up, so the ordering is fixed there too.
    has   ContributedOrder   std::vector<DeclaredRecording>  [-]  ?
    has   OrderedRecordings  std::vector<DeclaredRecording>  [-]  ?
    has   OrderingFixed      bool                            [-]  ?
    by    Source/ConsoleHost.cpp, Source/RenderSchedule.cpp
    note  🔴 The term is `RenderSchedule`. "Frame graph" is not a synonym: `Frame` is banned and "graph"

